WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.800
Sand on a steel plate, shaken at one frequency at a time.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.500
A square of steel, free at every edge, swept up to its first resonance at 56.8 Hz.

3
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:18.000
Where the plate moves, sand is thrown up. Where it stays still, sand collects.

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Each resonance has its own still lines, its nodal lines. Same plate, different frequency.

5
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Higher resonances, more lines.

6
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:57.000
A disc of the same steel. Its still lines are diameters and circles.

7
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:10.000
These are Chladni figures, after Ernst Chladni, who published them in 1787.

8
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:23.000
Every figure here is computed from the physics of a thin plate. Nothing draws the lines but the sand.

9
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:28.800
Sound, made visible.
